% Content cut into streams in the middle of q ... cm ... Q, so that a stream
% ends at another CTM than it began with (see
% EPDFContentRewriteEmbedderTest.KeepsContentCutIntoStreams).
%
% The text sits off whole pixels at a pixel per point. The text left after a
% redaction starts a text object of its own, placed to within float rounding
% of where it was, and PDFium draws a glyph that lies on a pixel edge on
% either side of it.
%
% Page 0: the shape "Microsoft: Print To PDF" writes. One cm at the top of
% the first stream flips and scales the whole page and is never undone; the
% content is then cut into streams wherever a size limit falls, here in the
% middle of a path inside q ... cm ... Q each time. Every stream after the
% first so begins and ends at a different CTM.
10 0 obj << /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 300 200]
  /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >>
  /Contents [11 0 R 12 0 R 13 0 R 14 0 R] >>
endobj
11 0 obj << /Length 118 >>
stream
.75 0 0 -.75 0 200 cm
BT /F1 16 Tf 1 0 0 -1 21 41 Tm (keep SECRET keep) Tj ET
q
1 0 0 1 40 80 cm
0 0 0 rg
0 0 m
60 0 l
endstream
endobj
